    "summary": "Charcoal drawing on machine-made paper, showing a woman seated on a cane-back chair and reading a book. To the side are two sketches of a little boy, dressed only in a T-shirt, amusing himself and a sketch of the head of the same child. The woman is wearing a traditional Vietnamese &#039;ao dai&#039;, a long side-fastening gown with slits up either side seam to the hips, over loose trousers and with flat sandals. Her hair is tied in a loose chignon at the nape of her neck after the fashion of married women. Signed, dated and inscribed.",
